Z||000007||1FST2M6||08-22-2001||01:46 PM||||ME (Mechanical engineering) degree (spent more than half my time in the thermodynamics and internal combustion labs) at Georgia Tech that turned into hydrodynamics and conceptual Golf Course modeling and property water management. Which is what i'm doing now. <P>the models of a course holes you see on ESPN and the Golf Channel... i do that. as well as monitor Irrigations systems at Resorts like Sandestin <A HREF="http://www.sandestin.com" TARGET=_blank>www.sandestin.com</A>  and other larger scale multi use propertys. (Commercial, Resort and Golf) no residential. (i don't get dirty.. just sit behind a monitor all day.) <P> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||thomas_l||08-22-2001||01:52 PM||||After 3 years to get started and another 4 to finish, I got a BBA in Computer Information Systems at Georgia State. I am a program manager at a global I/T services company. Now I get to work on cars as a hobby instead of an occupation  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
