Z||000026||WampusCat||08-22-2001||08:46 PM||||Did a pre-engineering program at a jr. college, AS in "general studies".  Then did one year in Mech Eng. at U.of S.Alabama, ran out of money, dropped out and joined the Marines.  After two years as a clerk/typist, got accepted to OCS, went flight program and wound up as a Harrier pilot.  Got a BS from Embry Riddle in my  spare time in 'Professional Aeronautics', whatever that means.  Currently flying right seat of A-320 for Northwest Airlines.  <BR>  My brother-in-law who went to trade school and got his welding cert. made more money than I did last year and enjoys his job in paper-mill maint. as much as I enjoy mine so you just never know what's going to work out or make you happy.  <BR>  I don't regret any of the 13.5 years I spent in the 'corps, but I'm glad to be a long haired civilian again!||||reg||1
